WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.850 --> 00:00:05.940
You can imagine when we want to boost
our well-being we often seek out these

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:09.690
really beautiful places, but the problem
is how do you measure these beautiful

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:14.099
places? And that's not been an easy thing
to do. So luckily, I came across this

00:00:14.099 --> 00:00:17.730
website and it's this online game people
play, and it's really simple. You just

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:21.390
rate these images between 1 and 10.
What's happening in the background is

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:24.779
that each image represents a square
kilometer of the United Kingdom. So I've

00:00:24.779 --> 00:00:28.859
got like over 200,000 images that have been
weighted about 1.5 million times.

00:00:28.859 --> 00:00:33.059
So I'm using Azure to train my deep
learning models because I really need

00:00:33.059 --> 00:00:38.399
GPU access. What's really great about
using Azure is that I can train models in

00:00:38.399 --> 00:00:41.850
a matter of days which normally would
take months on my desktop. So our

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:47.190
research also seeks to measure aspects
of the world that we as humans have

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:51.390
always been hugely aware of but that
traditionally we've had near to no

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:56.280
numbers on. I think an excellent example
of this is the beauty of environments

00:00:56.280 --> 00:01:01.500
that we spend our time in. So I think
many of us have this impression that

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:05.970
that's something which can have a real
impact on our day-to-day well-being. So

00:01:05.970 --> 00:01:09.380
we do find that people are happier in
these more beautiful environments and

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:13.350
they can be these beautiful natural
scenes, but I was really surprised to

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:17.040
find that people are also happier in
more beautiful city environments. And

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:20.610
people actually do find buildings as
being beautiful as well.

00:01:20.610 --> 00:01:24.570
So I'm really excited about the
possibilities of data science because I

00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:29.360
strongly believe that data science will
change the world for the better.

